.TH MYSTRNCPY 3 "September 2026" "Version 0.4.1" "myutils Library"
.SH NAME
mystrncpy \- copy a bounded number of characters from a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "#include \(dqmystrfunctions.h\(dq"
.sp
.BI "int mystrncpy(char *" dest ", const char *" src ", int " n );
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR mystrncpy ()
function copies at most
.I n
characters from the string pointed to by
.I src
into the buffer pointed to by
.IR dest .
If
.I src
is shorter than
.IR n ,
the remainder of
.I dest
is padded with null bytes, matching the behaviour of the standard
.BR strncpy (3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, the number of characters actually copied from
.I src
is returned. If
.IR dest ", " src
is NULL, or
.I n
is negative, \-1 is returned.
